  🔧 LAYER 1 — THE ANALOGY BANK
Lock these in. When you see a problem — the analogy fires instantly.
  SET         → Bouncer's stamp log
              "Have I seen this face before?"
              YES/NO. Nothing else.

DICT        → Phone book
              "Give me Ravi's number"
              Key → Value. Direct lookup.

COUNTER     → Tally chart
              "How many times did this appear?"
              Frequency. Count. That's it.

DEFAULTDICT → Phone book that auto-creates pages
              "Group things under a key"
              Never throws KeyError.

LIST        → Numbered lockers
              "Give me locker #3"
              Position matters. Direct access.

STACK       → Plates on a table
              Last plate in = First plate out
              LIFO. Undo. Brackets. State.

QUEUE       → Ticket counter line
              First person in = First served
              FIFO. BFS. Level order.

MONO STACK  → Waiting room
              Each element waits for answer
              Pop when answer found
              Push when still waiting

HEAP        → Hospital emergency room
              Most critical patient always first
              Min heap = least critical first
              Max heap = most critical first

LINKED LIST → Treasure hunt
              Each clue points to next
              No jumping. Must follow chain.

TREE        → Family tree
              Parent has two children
              Recursion = natural traversal

BST         → Dictionary book
              Left page = smaller words
              Right page = larger words
              O(log n) search always

BINARY SEARCH → Dictionary lookup
              Open middle → go left or right
              Eliminate half each step

TWO POINTERS → Two fingers on array
              Move based on condition
              Array never changes

SLIDING WINDOW → Cardboard frame
              Move frame across frozen array
              L and R are just boundaries

PREFIX SUM  → Car odometer
              Accumulates. Never resets.
              Build once → answer forever

MERGE SORT  → Divide army then conquer
              Split → sort each half → merge

QUICK SORT  → Pick a leader (pivot)
              Smaller left, larger right
              Leader in correct position

INTERVALS   → Timeline of meetings
              Sort by start → process left to right
