  🔑 LAYER 3 — THE ONE-LINE RULES
These are the rules that solve problems instantly
  WEEK 1:
  dict/set lookup    = O(1) always
  list search        = O(n) always
  Two separate loops = O(n) not O(n²)
  Trade space for time = dict/set

WEEK 2:
  R - L + 1         = window size
  Fixed window       = "size k" in problem
  Variable window    = "longest/shortest"
  Shrink when MET    = minimise problems
  Shrink when BROKEN = maximise problems
  prefix[R+1]-prefix[L] = range sum O(1)

WEEK 3:
  Stack top          = stack[-1] in Python
  Monotonic stack    = O(n) despite while loop
                       each element in+out once
  BFS uses queue     = FIFO natural for levels
  len(queue) at start = exact nodes this level

WEEK 4:
  Dummy node         = return dummy.next always
  Three pointers     = save → reverse → move
  Slow/fast middle   = fast 2x → slow at middle
  Recursion cost     = O(n) hidden stack space
  Floyd phase 2      = reset slow → move both 1

WEEK 5:
  Tree template      = if not node → return base
                       left = solve(left)
                       right = solve(right)
                       return combine
  BST inorder        = sorted order always
  Validate BST       = pass min/max boundaries
                       NOT just check children
  left <= right      = handles single element
  Rotated array      = ONE half always sorted
  BFS shortest path  = always BFS not DFS

WEEK 6:
  Merge sort         = O(n log n) ALWAYS
  Quick sort         = O(n²) worst case
  K largest          = MIN heap size K
  K smallest         = MAX heap size K
  heap[0]            = Kth largest always
  Median stream      = two heaps balanced
  Intervals          = SORT BY START FIRST
  Non-overlapping    = sort by END instead
  Meeting rooms      = heap stores END TIMES
                       heap size = rooms needed
